                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A very asterisk-heavy *conditional* recommend. It's a cute and functional typing game. HOWEVER, it is VERY light on content. Currently consists of three levels and an Endless Mode. Response time is snappy and the word library is decent for the amount of current content available. The included color swatches are a nice extra.\n\nMy playtime for 100% was about 20 minutes -- two or three of which was spent taking 100 screenshots for the final achievement. Perhaps if you're not a particularly skilled typist, you might end up spending more time in Endless Mode, but I only had to play through it once. Any time beyond that (at least until the next content update) will likely be for trading cards.\n\nIt was launched in 2017, but was dropped for a while and then picked back up in 2024. Updates (although mostly small) seem to be fairly regular since then. Unless you really just want to throw the dev a fiver though, I can't in good conscience recommend paying full price for this. That being said, if you like the idea of supporting a solo dev who is providing steady updates, it is often discounted to around a dollar. Not the worst thing you could spend 100 pennies on.",
